# Socrate admin console · SPA environment configuration
# Optional: copy this file to .env.local (git-ignored; Vite loads it) to override a value.
# The BFF has its own template in bff/.env.example.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend-for-Frontend (BFF) model
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SPA is a PURE COOKIE CLIENT. It holds NO tokens and NO OAuth client
# config: the BFF (see bff/) is the confidential OAuth client. It runs the
# Authorization Code + PKCE flow server-side, keeps the tokens in a server-side
# session, and the browser only ever holds an opaque HttpOnly session cookie.
#
# In production, Caddy serves the SPA and reverse-proxies an allowlist to the
# BFF on the same origin (`/bff/*`, `/api/admin/*`, `/api/apps/*`, `/api/profile`,
# `GET /api/version` and the two password-reset posts) — so the SPA talks to ITS
# OWN origin and these vars are normally left UNSET (same-origin defaults).
# See deploy/.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Admin API origin. Leave UNSET for the same-origin BFF deployment (the SPA
# calls relative `/api/admin/*` and the BFF injects the bearer). Set to an
# absolute HTTPS origin only for split-origin setups. MUST be https:// in prod.
#   • same-origin (BFF):  (leave unset)
# VITE_ADMIN_API_URL=

# Public OIDC issuer origin. src/utils/secureConfig.ts parses it and refuses a
# non-https:// value in production builds, but no request uses it today: the
# forgot/reset-password posts go through the BFF on the same origin. Leave UNSET.
#   • production (if ever needed):  https://socrate.example.com
# VITE_OIDC_ISSUER=

# Base path of the built assets (vite.config.ts). The SPA is served at the root
# of its host; set only for a sub-path deployment.
# VITE_BASE=/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev (npm run dev)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Vite dev server proxies `/bff/*` and `/api/admin/*` to a locally-running
# BFF on :8091 (run the BFF from bff/ with its own .env), and the public issuer
# flows (`/api/auth/*`, `/api/profile`, `/oauth/*`) to the backend on :8080.
# With that topology in place, both vars above stay unset in dev too.
